# Hostname egress allowlist for the infra dev-container profile.
#
# One pattern per line; `#` starts a comment. A pattern is a hostname, or a
# hostname whose FIRST label carries `*` wildcards (`*.githubusercontent.com`,
# `productionresultssa*.blob.core.windows.net`). init-egress-proxy.sh rejects
# any other shape -- a wildcard in a later label, a bare `*`, a pattern with no
# dot, or a wildcard label sitting directly on a TLD -- and refuses to start the
# proxy rather than assembling a list that admits more than it reads as.
#
# Matching is tinyproxy's `FilterType fnmatch` against the CONNECT host, so a
# pattern with no `*` matches that host and nothing else: `example.com` does not
# admit `notexample.com`, the way an unanchored regular expression would.
# fnmatch is case-sensitive, so every pattern here is lowercase and a client
# that spells a host in uppercase is denied -- the safe direction.
#
# The proxy is the SECOND egress lane. The first is init-firewall.sh's IP
# allowlist, which the infra profile leaves exactly as the default profile has
# it; the hosts it already admits are repeated at the bottom of this file so
# that this file is a complete statement of the profile's reach, and so that
# SSH (which is routed through the proxy for every destination) can reach
# github.com.
#
# PSILINK_EGRESS_EXTRA_HOSTS in the repository-root .env adds a comma-separated
# list of further patterns at container start, for a zone name or an instance
# address that should not be a repository change.

# --- AWS, by service endpoint ----------------------------------------------
#
# Deliberately NOT `*.amazonaws.com`. That wildcard would admit
# `*.compute.amazonaws.com` -- the public DNS name of every AWS customer's EC2
# instance -- and so re-open by name exactly the shared-tenant channel the IP
# allowlist cannot close. Each service endpoint is named instead. The region is
# us-west-2, matching infra/aws_eb and apps/web/deploy/aws_eb.
#
# Every hostname down to route53 below is what `aws <service> <op> --region
# us-west-2 --debug` resolved, not what the service is called: the CLI puts
# cost explorer on `ce.us-east-1`, service quotas on `servicequotas` with no
# hyphen, CloudWatch on `monitoring`, and the marketplace catalog on
# `catalog.marketplace.<region>` rather than any of the obvious spellings.
sts.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
ec2.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
iam.amazonaws.com
budgets.amazonaws.com
ce.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
servicequotas.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
apigateway.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
lambda.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
dynamodb.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
logs.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
monitoring.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
cloudformation.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
catalog.marketplace.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
elasticbeanstalk.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
ssm.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
route53.amazonaws.com

# The legacy global STS endpoint, and the two Session Manager data-plane hosts
# the SSM agent and the session-manager-plugin open rather than the CLI. No
# `aws` invocation resolves any of these, so unlike the block above they are
# taken from their service's documented `<service>.<region>.amazonaws.com`
# shape; each is an AWS-operated name, none is a customer namespace.
sts.amazonaws.com
ssmmessages.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
ec2messages.us-west-2.amazonaws.com

# Plain HTTPS hosts rather than API endpoints.
ip-ranges.amazonaws.com
checkip.amazonaws.com
docs.aws.amazon.com

# Stated residual: the two entries below are themselves CUSTOMER namespaces, not
# AWS-operated hostnames. Any account's bucket answers on
# `<bucket>.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com`, and any account's API Gateway stage
# answers on `<api-id>.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com`, so admitting the
# wildcards admits a channel to storage and to an HTTP endpoint an adversary
# controls. They are admitted deliberately -- virtual-hosted-style S3 is how the
# aws CLI addresses a bucket, and the deployed web app's API is reached this way
# -- and accepted as a residual rather than closed. `*.compute.amazonaws.com` is
# the same shape and is NOT admitted, because nothing here needs it.
s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
*.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com
*.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com

